    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279-a2">

                <pb facs="0327" n="1061" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1061"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Peterson to Mr. Waix.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial Russian Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1895-06-27"><hi rendition="#italic">June 27,
                                1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of June 26,
                    inclosing passport and $1.20, I would inform you that before your passport can
                    be viséed you must inform me where you were born and what your religion is—if
                    Christain or Jew.</p>
                <p>I shall retain your passport and fee unil receipt of your answer.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. G. Peterson</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vice-Consul.</hi><lb/>(For the Consul-General.)</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
